Debugging Implications
Because optimizations change the structure and order of the compiled code, a program that runs correctly with -O0 but fails with -O1 almost certainly contains a bug that should be fixed. Using a debug-specific optimization level like -Og (optimizes for debugging experience) or using tools like AddressSanitizer (ASAN) and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer (UBSAN) with appropriate flags (they often recommend -O1 for best results) can help pinpoint the exact source of these underlying issues. 
